, 											{
												"box" : 												{
													"fontname" : "Arial",
													"fontsize" : 11.0,
													"id" : "obj-541",
													"linecount" : 9,
													"maxclass" : "comment",
													"numinlets" : 1,
													"numoutlets" : 0,
													"patching_rect" : [ 282.0, 608.0, 417.0, 117.0 ],
													"text" : "This device uses the retune~ object in a polyphonic patch structure, thus allowing some multiple harmonizations. The DSP part of the patch is embedded into a poly~ container, that lets you load an open number of instances of a patcher file, and thus allows the use of polyphonic audio synthesis, audio processing or even control tasks. The patcher file loaded into the poly~ container has an auto-muting system which is used to spare some CPU consumption, as the number of played voices increases. Harmonization chords can be set using a MIDI input when the device is used in Max. In Live, we use a special MIDI-side-chaining device, called \"Max MIDI Send\", in order to send some MIDI data to other devices such as the present one."
												}

											}
