, 											{
												"box" : 												{
													"annotation" : "Inverts the right-channel signal relative to the left-channel signal. The delayed signals (one for the upper band, one for the lower band) are sent to both output channels. If the Invert button is pressed, the right channel is inverted (multiplied by –1). This gives a nice stereo spread because the delayed signals are inverted with respect to each other, and also because they cause different cancellations with the dry signal.",
